{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>At eventide.</b> In the evening the people of Jerusalem were afraid of him." "<b> terror.</b> Like בלהות אתנך (Ezekiel 26:21). The meaning of בלהות is הלהות (terrifying), inverted, like כשב and כבש (Leviticus 3:7 and 4:32)." "<b>Before morning and he is not.</b> When the angel went forth and annihilated most of the camp." "<b>This is the portion of those who plunder us.</b> The words of the prophet, and he rejoices."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:09.353363234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}